quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  5,37,"They will wish to come out from the Fire, but they shall never be able to leave it, and there is a lasting punishment for them."
  5,38,"As for the male and female thieves, cut off their hands as a requital for what they have done. (That is) an exemplary punishment from Allah. And Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  5,39,"But whoever repents after his wrongdoing and reforms (himself), then Allah shall accept his repentance. Indeed, Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  5,40,Do you not know that to Allah belongs the kingdom of the heavens and the earth? He punishes whomever He wills and forgives whomever He pleases. And Allah is All-Capable of everything.
  5,41,"O Messenger! Let them not grieve you, those who hasten in (promoting) disbelief, those who say: ‘We believe’ with their mouths, but their hearts do not believe. Nor, those among the Jews who listen eagerly intending (to tell) lies (about you) to others who have not yet come to you, (and they) distort the words from their meanings (and contexts), and say (to each other): ‘If you are given this (particular ruling), then take it, but if you are not given this, then beware!’ And whomever Allah intends to try (by error or temptation), you cannot avail him anything against Allah. They are the ones whose hearts Allah did not desire to purify. For them is disgrace in this world, and there is a grievous punishment for them in the Hereafter."
